"```python\n# cython: boundscheck=False, wraparound=False\n# cython: language_level=3\n\ncdef extern from \"hash.h\":\n    int hash_int(int x)\n    int hash_str(char* x)\n\ncdef int ksuid_keygen(int key):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate a unique identifier for a given key using the KSUID algorithm.\n    \n    This function combines hashing and encoding techniques to produce a unique identifier.\n    The hashing function is based on the built-in hash_int function, which returns a hash value.\n    The encoding function is based on the built-in hash_str function, which returns a hash value.\n    The final hash value is then encoded using the base64 library to produce a unique identifier.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Initialize the hash value with the key\n    hash_value = hash_int(key)\n    \n    # Encode the hash value using base64\n    encoded_value = base64.b64encode(hash_value)\n    \n    # Return the encoded value\n    return encoded_value\n\n# Example usage:\nkey = b\"example_key\"\nksuid_id = ksuid_keygen(key)\nprint(ksuid_id)\n```"
"```python\nimport sentry\n\ndef configure_sentry_logging():\n    \"\"\"\n    Configures Sentry to capture and send log messages from the application.\n    \"\"\"\n    sentry.init(\n        dsn=\"https://your-sentry-dsn.com\",  # Replace with your Sentry DSN\n        traces_sample_rate=1.0  # 100% sample rate\n    )\n\n# Example usage:\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    configure_sentry_logging()\n```\n\nPlease note that you need to replace `https://your-sentry-dsn.com` with your actual Sentry DSN (Data Source Name). You can obtain a DSN by creating a project in the Sentry dashboard and generating a JSON Web Token (JWT) that you can use in your application."
