"```python\nimport pytest\n\nclass BatchRunner:\n    def __init__(self, test_cases):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the batch runner with a list of test cases.\n        \n        Args:\n        test_cases (list): A list of test cases to be run in batches.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.test_cases = test_cases\n\n    def run_tests(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Run the test cases in batches and provide incremental feedback.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Use a for loop to iterate over the test cases in batches of 5\n        for i, test_case in enumerate(self.test_cases, start=1):\n            print(f\"Running test case {i}...\")\n            # Run the test case and store the result\n            result = test_case()\n            # Provide incremental feedback based on the test result\n            if result:\n                print(\" PASSED!\")\n            else:\n                print(\" FAILED!\")\n            # Print the test case number and result for clarity\n            print(f\"Test case {i}: {result}\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Define a list of test cases\n    test_cases = [\n        # Test case 1\n        lambda: \"This is test case 1\",\n        # Test case 2\n        lambda: \"This is test case 2\",\n        # Test case 3\n        lambda: \"This is test case 3\"\n    ]\n\n    # Create a batch runner with the test cases\n    batch_runner = BatchRunner(test_cases)\n\n    # Run the tests in batches\n    batch_runner.run_tests()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```"
"```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\nclass ExperimentFramework:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.experiments = None\n        self.dataframes = None\n\n    def create_experiment(self, experiment_name, experiment_data):\n        \"\"\"\n        Create a new experiment.\n\n        Args:\n            experiment_name (str): The name of the experiment.\n            experiment_data (dict): A dictionary containing the experiment data.\n        \"\"\"\n        if self.experiments is None:\n            self.experiments = []\n        \n        new_experiment = {\n            \"name\": experiment_name,\n            \"data\": experiment_data\n        }\n        self.experiments.append(new_experiment)\n\n    def search_experiments(self, query):\n        \"\"\"\n        Search for experiments by name or data.\n\n        Args:\n            query (str): The query to search for.\n\n        Returns:\n            list: A list of experiments that match the query.\n        \"\"\"\n        results = []\n        for experiment in self.experiments:\n            if query.lower() in str(experiment).lower():\n                results.append(experiment)\n        return results\n\n    def compare_experiments(self, experiment1, experiment2):\n        \"\"\"\n        Compare two experiments.\n\n        Args:\n            experiment1 (dict): The first experiment.\n            experiment2 (dict): The second experiment.\n\n        Returns:\n            dict: A dictionary containing the comparison results.\n        \"\"\"\n        comparison = {}\n        for key, value in experiment1.items():\n            if key in experiment2:\n                comparison[key] = value == experiment2[key]\n            else:\n                comparison[key] = False\n        return comparison\n\n    def save_experiments(self, filename):\n        \"\"\"\n        Save the experiments to a file.\n\n        Args:\n            filename (str): The filename to save the experiments to.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.experiments_df = pd.DataFrame(self.experiments)\n        self.experiments_df.to_csv(filename, index=False)\n\n    def load_experiments(self, filename):\n        \"\"\"\n        Load the experiments from a file.\n\n        Args:\n            filename (str): The filename to load the experiments from.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.experiments_df = pd.read_csv(filename, index_col=False)\n\n# Example usage\nframework = ExperimentFramework()\nframework.create_experiment(\"Experiment1\", {\"input\": np.random.rand(1000), \"output\": np.random.rand(1000)})\nframework.create_experiment(\"Experiment2\", {\"input\": np.random.rand(1000), \"output\": np.random.rand(1000)})\n\nquery = \"Experiment1\"\nresults = framework.search_experiments(query)\nprint(\"Experiments matching the query:\", results)\n\nexperiment1 = {\"input\": np.random.rand(1000), \"output\": np.random.rand(1000)}\nexperiment2 = {\"input\": np.random.rand(1000), \"output\": np.random.rand(1000)}\ncomparison = framework.compare_experiments(experiment1, experiment2)\nprint(\"Comparison results:\", comparison)\n\nframework.save_experiments(\"experiments.csv\")\n```\n\nThis framework provides a basic structure for easily recording, searching, and comparing AI experiments. It uses a dictionary to store experiments, where each experiment is represented by a dictionary containing the input and output data. The framework provides methods for creating new experiments, searching for experiments by name or data, comparing two experiments, saving the experiments to a file, and loading the experiments from a file. The example usage demonstrates how to create experiments, search for experiments, compare two experiments, save the experiments to a file, and load the experiments from a file."
