"```python\n# Import necessary libraries\nfrom hadoop import MapReduce, Job, Text, IntWritable, LongWritable\nfrom hadoop.mapreduce import SimpleReducer\n\n# Define a MapReduce job\nclass MapReduceJob:\n    def __init__(self, input_file, output_file):\n        self.input_file = input_file\n        self.output_file = output_file\n\n    def map(self, key, values):\n        # Map function: process each key-value pair\n        return [IntWritable(value) for value in values]\n\n    def reduce(self, key, values):\n        # Reduce function: group key with its values\n        return LongWritable(key)\n\n    def configure(self, jobconf):\n        # Configure job parameters\n        jobconf.setJobName(\"mapreduce_job\")\n        jobconf.setJarByName(\"mapreduce_job\")\n        jobconf.setMapperClass(\"com.example.MapReduceMapper\")\n        jobconf.setReducerClass(\"com.example.Reducer\")\n        jobconf.setCombinerClass(None)\n        jobconf.setMapOutputKeyClass(Text.class)\n        jobconf.setMapOutputValueClass(IntWritable.class)\n        jobconf.setReducerInputClass(Text.class)\n        jobconf.setReducerOutputClass(Text.class)\n\n    def execute(self, jobconf):\n        # Execute the job on a Hadoop cluster\n        job = Job(jobconf)\n        job.setJarByName(\"mapreduce_job\")\n        job.setMapperClass(self.map)\n        job.setReducerClass(self.reduce)\n        job.configure(jobconf)\n        job.setInputFiles(self.input_file)\n        job.setOutputFiles(self.output_file)\n        job.submit()\n\n\n# Create a MapReduce job\ninput_file = \"input.txt\"\noutput_file = \"output.txt\"\njob = MapReduceJob(input_file, output_file)\n\n# Configure the job\njob.configure(None)\n\n# Execute the job\njob.execute(None)\n```\n\nThis Python code defines a `MapReduceJob` class that implements a MapReduce job using the Hadoop API. The job reads data from a file (`input.txt`), processes it using the `map` function, and writes the result to a new file (`output.txt`). The job is configured with the necessary parameters, including the input and output files, and the mapper and reducer classes. The job is then executed on a Hadoop cluster using the `submit()` method."
