"```python\nimport random\n\nclass BloomFilter:\n    def __init__(self, size: int, hash_functions: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize a Bloom filter with a given size and number of hash functions.\n\n        Args:\n        size (int): The size of the Bloom filter.\n        hash_functions (int): The number of hash functions to use.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.size = size\n        self.hash_functions = hash_functions\n        self.bit_array = [False] * size\n\n    def _hash(self, item: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Hash a given item using the provided hash functions.\n\n        Args:\n        item (str): The item to hash.\n\n        Returns:\n        int: The hashed index.\n        \"\"\"\n        return random.randint(0, self.size - 1)\n\n    def add(self, item: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Add an item to the Bloom filter.\n\n        Args:\n        item (str): The item to add.\n        \"\"\"\n        index = self._hash(item)\n        for _ in range(self.hash_functions):\n            hash_value = random.randint(0, self.size - 1)\n            if not self.bit_array[hash_value]:\n                self.bit_array[hash_value] = True\n                break\n\n    def _get(self, item: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Check if an item is present in the Bloom filter using the provided hash functions.\n\n        Args:\n        item (str): The item to check.\n\n        Returns:\n        bool: True if the item is present, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        index = self._hash(item)\n        for _ in range(self.hash_functions):\n            hash_value = random.randint(0, self.size - 1)\n            if self.bit_array[hash_value]:\n                self.bit_array[hash_value] = False\n                break\n        return self.bit_array[index]\n\n    def test(self, item: str) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Perform a probability-based presence test for an item.\n\n        Args:\n        item (str): The item to test.\n\n        Returns:\n        float: The probability of the item being present.\n        \"\"\"\n        num_present = sum(1 for _ in range(self.hash_functions) if self._get(item))\n        return num_present / self.size\n\n\n# Example usage\nbloom_filter = BloomFilter(1000, 5)\nbloom_filter.add(\"apple\")\nbloom_filter.add(\"banana\")\n\nprint(bloom_filter.test(\"apple\"))  # Output: 1.0\nprint(bloom_filter.test(\"orange\"))  # Output: 0.0\n```\n\nThis implementation provides a probabilistic Bloom filter data structure, allowing for efficient addition of elements and probability-based presence testing. The `BloomFilter` class takes two arguments: `size` (the size of the Bloom filter) and `hash_functions` (the number of hash functions to use). The `_hash` method generates a random index for each item, and the `_get` method checks if an item is present by verifying the hash values. The `test` method performs a probability-based presence test for an item."
