"```python\nimport requests\n\n# Function to fetch HTML tag names from a reputable source\ndef get_html_tags(url):\n    \"\"\"\n    Fetches HTML tag names from a given URL and returns them as a list.\n    \n    Args:\n        url (str): The URL of the HTML documentation page.\n    \n    Returns:\n        list: A list of HTML tag names.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Send a GET request to the URL and get the HTML response\n    response = requests.get(url)\n    \n    # Check if the request was successful\n    if response.status_code != 200:\n        raise Exception(f\"Failed to retrieve HTML tags. Status code: {response.status_code}\")\n    \n    # Parse the HTML content using BeautifulSoup\n    from bs4 import BeautifulSoup\n    soup = BeautifulSoup(response.content, 'html.parser')\n    \n    # Find all HTML tag names in the parsed HTML\n    tags = soup.find_all(True)\n    \n    # Extract the tag names from the tags\n    tag_names = [tag.name for tag in tags]\n    \n    return tag_names\n\n# Get the list of HTML tag names from the Mozilla Developer Network\nmoz_tags = get_html_tags('https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Tag_names')\nprint(\"Mozilla Developer Network Tag Names:\")\nprint(moz_tags)\n\n# Get the list of HTML tag names from the W3Schools documentation\nw3schools_tags = get_html_tags('https://www.w3schools.com/html/')\nprint(\"\\nW3Schools Documentation Tag Names:\")\nprint(w3schools_tags)\n```\n\nPlease note that the above code might not work directly as the list of HTML tag names is not static and is constantly changing. However, the above code is a simple way to fetch the list of HTML tag names from a given URL."
